flowchart TB
    accTitle: The catalog bot
    accDescr: Every Monday, or when started by hand, the Catalog workflow lists the repositories of the owner with gh, asks every website of a project at dennis-otto.github.io for its German version, and reads the file from which each card reads what its project works with and the screenshot and the logo from which the hub draws its German picture, on the default branch of its repository. .github/mkdocs_project.py --network compares them with projects.toml. When something differs, the bot opens or updates the issue The project catalog is out of date, and a person changes projects.toml and writes the table of the README. When nothing differs, the bot closes the issue.

    week(["Every Monday<br>or by hand"])
    repos["gh repo list<br>the repositories of the owner"]
    sites["The website of every project<br>and its folder de/"]
    files["The files of every project<br>that say what it works with<br>and draw its German picture"]
    catalog[("projects.toml")]
    compare[".github/mkdocs_project.py<br>--network"]
    issue["`The issue<br>*The project catalog is out of date*`"]
    fix(["A person changes projects.toml<br>and runs --write"])
    closed["The issue closes"]

    week --> repos & sites & files
    repos & sites & files & catalog --> compare
    compare -- "something differs" --> issue
    issue --> fix
    fix -.-> catalog
    compare -- "nothing differs" --> closed

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class week,repos,sites,compare bot
    class issue,fix person
    class closed done
